      "title": "WSP4606 N-Ch and P-Channel MOSFET"
    },
    "extraction_notes": [
      "The WSP4606 datasheet describes both N-channel and P-channel MOSFET characteristics. This extraction uses the N-channel polarity because the schema supports one polarity; the P-channel values are retained here for context: BVDSS -30 V, VGS(th) -1.0/-1.5/-2.5 V, RDS(ON) 30 mOhm typ at VGS=-10 V and 48 mOhm typ at VGS=-4.5 V, Ciss 645 pF, Coss 272 pF, Crss 105 pF, and VSD -1.2 V max at IS=-6 A.",
      "N-channel RDS(ON) maximums are 0.028 ohm at VGS = 10 V, ID = 6 A and 0.032 ohm at VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 5 A.",
      "N-channel gate charge is 7.2 nC at VGS endpoint 4.5 V; Qgs is 1.4 nC and Qgd is 2.2 nC at VDS = 20 V, ID = 6 A.",
      "N-channel body-diode continuous source-current maximum is 7 A and pulsed source-current maximum is 20 A.",
      "No transfer-characteristics curve is published; output, on-resistance, body-diode, gate-charge, and capacitance curves are available."
    ],
    "family": "mosfet",
    "manufacturer": "Winsok Semicon",
    "mpn": "WSP4606",
    "omission_reason": "The datasheet publishes no transfer ID-versus-VGS curve and no body-diode reverse-recovery time. The part contains both N-channel and P-channel devices, while this schema provides only one polarity slot; P-channel values are retained in extraction_notes.",
